  m_Name: M1_01_Welcome_Order_Picking
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Valari.Data.TutorialData
  <Title>k__BackingField: Welcome to Order Picking
  <Description>k__BackingField: Order picking is the process of retrieving specific
    products from their storage locations in the warehouse to fulfil a customer order.
    It is the most labour-intensive activity in any fulfilment operation, accounting
    for 50 to 75 percent of total warehouse operating costs. Picking accuracy directly
    affects customer satisfaction, every mis-pick results in a return, a reshipping
    cost, and a dissatisfied customer. In this module you will learn how to read
    a pick list, locate and verify the correct product, pick the correct quantity,
    and handle errors before they leave the warehouse floor.
  <VoiceOver>k__BackingField: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cd5a4de7994799741a2b38e1e1da20b7, type: 3}
